Process
-------

What is a process ?

A program which is under execution is called process. 

./a.out -> process running in foreground
./a.out& -> process running in background

when a process started execution process manager will provide the unique id called as pid.

$ ./a.out & 

[1] 59   ----> pid
 |
 |_____	 job id 
	

Using ps command will display the jobs under the particular terminal.
Using fg command will bring bacgkgroung job to foreground.

Daemon process : A Daemon process is special process that is created and handled by the system in the same way as other process.
		 Daemon process will start running once system booting completed, they terminate when system shutdown.
		 Many services are started as daemons.

		 fg jobid -> according to jobid particular process is getback a foreground
		 
		 if 2 or more process are running background and then we are using fg, then fg brings most recently backgrounded process to foreground. 		 		

Multiprocessing
---------------

1. Hardware multiprocessing
	
	in case of hardware multiprocessing for every application, seperate hardware (CPU) is presented.

	[app1]		[app2]		[app3]

	  |		  |		  |

	[--------------Kernel----------------]

	  |		  |		  |

	[cpu1]		[cpu2]		[cpu3]

	* Faster execution
	* Higher cost
	* Higher power consumption

2. Software multiprocessing
	
	in case of software multiprocessing all applications will run on a single CPU with help of OS.

	[app1]		[app2]		[app3]

	  |		  |		  |

	[-----------------OS-------------------]
		
			  |
	
	                [cpu]

	* Slower exection
	* Lower cose
	* Lower power consumption

